Initial PR CI: https://github.com/soren-labs/sbx-browser/actions/runs/37198186695
Backend failure: test_user_modal_runtime_direct_grants_and_reconstruction
Expected direct connection HTTP 200; observed HTTP 409 during runtime startup.

Root cause 1: a session and sandbox published between the sweep's durable
record listing and remote handle listing were classified as an orphan.
The orphan pass could terminate compute before startup finished binding it.

Before-fix deterministic reproduction:
test_rev001_create_after_sweep_listing_is_not_orphan_killed
creating/unbound: FAIL (compute terminated)
creating/bound: FAIL (compute terminated)
running/bound: FAIL (compute terminated)
idle/bound: FAIL (compute terminated)

Fix: read the durable owning record after handle enumeration. Preserve active
bindings and in-flight creates. An unavailable durable read cannot authorize
termination. True orphans and terminal cleanup remain covered by reaper tests.

Root cause 2: an idle scan could fall back to terminating compute after a new
turn superseded its checkpoint claim. Reject termination of current active
compute without a lifecycle claim. Remote termination stays outside the plane
lock; accepted prompts stay durable while a checkpoint claim is active.

Regression: test_rev001_new_turn_supersedes_stale_idle_termination
New running turn and live compute both survive the stale sweep: PASS.

